@page "/getting-started"
<PageTitle>Getting started · WindBlazor</PageTitle>

<div class="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-300">Tutorial 01</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold">Getting started</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">The project is pre-release. Until an official package is published, reference the Razor Class Library from the repository.</p>
    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8">
        <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">1. Add a project reference</h2>
            <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-[#111a2d] p-5 text-sm text-cyan-100"><code>&lt;ProjectReference Include="..\WindBlazor\WindBlazor.csproj" /&gt;</code></pre>
        </section>
        <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">2. Import the Button namespace</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">In your consuming app's <code>_Imports.razor</code>:</p>
            <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-[#111a2d] p-5 text-sm text-cyan-100"><code>@@using WindBlazor.Components.Button</code></pre>
        </section>
        <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">3. Configure CSS-first Tailwind v4</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Include the app and library as explicit sources (paths relative to your CSS file):</p>
            <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-[#111a2d] p-5 text-sm text-cyan-100"><code>@@import "tailwindcss" source(none);
@@source "../../Components";
@@source "../../../WindBlazor/Components";</code></pre>
            <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-[#111a2d] p-5 text-sm text-cyan-100"><code>tailwindcss -i ./wwwroot/css/tailwind.css -o ./wwwroot/css/app.css --watch</code></pre>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Load generated <code>css/app.css</code> in your Blazor host. The standalone CLI must be on PATH.</p>
        </section>
        <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">4. Render a Button</h2>
            <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-[#111a2d] p-5 text-sm text-cyan-100"><code>&lt;Button Class="rounded bg-sky-500 px-4 py-2 text-white"&gt;Save&lt;/Button&gt;</code></pre>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-amber-200">The published repository currently exposes <code>Class</code>, not yet the planned <code>Css</code> API.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
    <a href="components/button" class="mt-10 inline-block rounded-xl bg-cyan-400 px-5 py-3 font-bold text-slate-950 hover:bg-cyan-300">See Button examples →</a>
</div>
